message.content:
Play-Doh modeling compound is classified in HTSUS 3407.00 ("modeling pastes; dental wax...; preparations with a basis of plaster"). Statistical suffix: 3407.00.20 is "Modeling pastes, put up in sets, or in packings for retail sale, or in plates, horseshoe shapes, sticks or similar forms," and 3407.00.40 covers other items.

Play-Doh sets are commonly classified under 3407.00.20.00 as modeling pastes put up for retail sale. That said, the set could be viewed as a toy set under 9503.00 instead. CBP rulings on Play-Doh sets with accessories often hold that, as a GRI 3(b) set, the essential character is the modeling compound, which gives 3407.00.20.00. The description stresses that the compound defines the set's nature, so I'm going with 3407.00.20.00.

{"hts_code": "3407.00.2000", "reason": "The set is put up for retail sale, and under GRI 3(b) the Play-Doh modeling compound gives it its essential character, so it is classified as modeling paste in heading 3407, with the plastic accessories subordinate."}
